From 15816fe1cbbb7f84f6a53ae0617b3189b3be1fd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:58:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui,app): an async file picker opens models and projects
 in the browser

The browser build (wasm32) had no way to open anything: every picker
answered "cancelled". File > Open model and Open project now ask a
browser <input type=file> (ui::file_pick) and return at once; the file's
name and bytes reach an inbox that State::drain_actions takes each frame
as CommandKind::OpenPicked. A model lands through the new
ImportModel::from_bytes (the path import's laws - IGES/unknown extension,
size cap, STEP budget bounds, finite-mesh gate - shared through
checked_budget) and finish_import, so it is one undo step; a project
through project::open_noted. A failed read, a file over the 256 MiB
browser read limit, a refused import or a non-text project is said on the
status line by name. Native builds keep rfd's synchronous dialogs; their
inbox stays empty.

Refs #31

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
